{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-29_ccc-ex99_1.htm, sha256 f3c99353295a099eea7aa78f8538bc9db1ad209675825c4862a4873d4212ee90.\nEX-99.1 2 ccc-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1\nCCC Intelligent Solutions Holdings Inc. Announces Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results\nOctober 29, 2026 \u2013 CCC Intelligent Solutions Holdings Inc. (\u201cCCC\u201d or the \u201cCompany\u201d) (NASDAQ: CCC), a leading SaaS and AI platform provider for the multi-trillion-dollar insurance economy, today announced its financial results for the three months ended September 30, 2026.\n\u201cCCC delivered strong third quarter results, with revenue growth of 10% and adjusted EBITDA margin of approximately 44%. Our performance reflects the durability of our business, the trust customers place in us, and the increasing role our platform plays in helping participants across the insurance economy operate more efficiently and achieve better outcomes,\u201d said Githesh Ramamurthy, Chairman & CEO of CCC.\n\u201cThe pending transaction with GTCR and Elliott marks an exciting next chapter for CCC and our customers,\u201d continued Ramamurthy. \u201cTogether, we expect to accelerate the AI and agentic capabilities our customers want from us, expand the network at the center of our platform, and make long-term investments in innovation that help customers navigate growing complexity across the claims lifecycle. We believe this positions CCC to deliver even greater value to the insurance economy in the years ahead.\u201d\nThird Quarter 2026 Financial Highlights\nRevenue\n\u2022 Total revenue was $294.1 million for the third quarter of 2026, an increase of 10.1% from $267.1 million for the third quarter of 2025.\nProfitability\n\u2022 GAAP gross profit was $218.0 million, representing a gross margin of 74%, for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $193.0 million, representing a gross margin of 72%, for the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted gross profit was $224.6 million, representing an adjusted gross profit margin of 76%, for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $199.5 million, representing an adjusted gross profit margin of 78%, for the third quarter of 2025. \u2022 GAAP operating income was $57.4 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with GAAP operating income of $30.0 million for the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted operating income was $115.7 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with adjusted operating income of $93.0 million for the third quarter of 2025. \u2022 GAAP net income was $30.2 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with GAAP net loss of $2.0 million for the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted net income was $75.1 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $59.4 million for the third quarter of 2025. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA was $130.5 million for the third quarter of 2026, up 18.5% compared with adjusted EBITDA of $110.1 million for the third quarter of 2025.\nLiquidity\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "\u2022 CCC had $202.9 million in cash and cash equivalents and $1.28 billion of total debt as of September 30, 2026. The Company generated $100.4 million in cash from operating activities and had free cash flow of $82.5 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $94.8 million in cash generated from operating activities and free cash flow of $78.6 million for the third quarter of 2025.\n3rd Quarter and Recent Business Highlights\n\u2022 GTCR and Elliott to acquire CCC. On October 15, 2026, CCC announced a definitive agreement to be acquired by a consortium of private investment firms led by GTCR and including Elliott Investment Management in an all-cash transaction in which shareholders will receive $7.75 per share, representing an enterprise value of approximately $6.1 billion. Subject to regulatory and stockholder approvals and other customary closing conditions, the proposed transaction is expected to close in the first quarter of 2027. Following the close, CCC will become a privately held company.\n\u2022 Insurers expand AI adoption across core claims workflows. CCC\u2019s AI-related revenue reached approximately $130 million in annualized run-rate in the third quarter of 2026, representing growth of 40% year over year and increasing from an annualized run rate of approximately $120 million in the second quarter of 2026. This growth reflects a continuing shift in customer behavior from AI experimentation to AI deployment at scale.\n\u2022 Leading insurer is largest to adopt Medhub for Auto Casualty. During the third quarter of 2026, a top-five insurer (based on 2025 direct premium written) became the largest insurer to adopt CCC\u2019s Medhub for Auto Casualty, which uses AI to extract critical insights from complex medical records and help claims professionals make faster, more informed decisions grounded in auditable claim data. The deployment marks the largest application of EvolutionIQ\u2019s technology within the P&C auto market and demonstrates customers\u2019 willingness to adopt adjacent workflows from CCC, underscoring the substantial growth opportunity beyond the traditional APD business.\nBusiness Outlook and Conference Call Information\nIn light of the proposed transaction, the Company is suspending its practice of providing guidance and will not be hosting a conference call or webcast to discuss the Company\u2019s financial results.\nAbout CCC Intelligent Solutions\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "CCC Intelligent Solutions Inc. (CCC), a subsidiary of CCC Intelligent Solutions Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: CCC), is a leading SaaS and AI platform provider powering the multi-trillion-dollar insurance and repair economy. CCC connects more than 35,000 businesses, including insurers, repairers, automakers and parts suppliers, through the workflows where claims and repair decisions are made every day. With AI built into those workflows for over a decade and informed by more than 40 years of industry data, CCC helps customers manage growing complexity and move work forward with confidence. Through purposeful innovation and the strength of its network, CCC helps keep people\u2019s lives moving forward when it matters most. Learn more about CCC at www.cccis.com.\nForward Looking Statements\n"}
